   "inputs": {
    "doc": "E-023 arm: stencil:9 RING r=222 km, seed 0 \u2014 the same nine slots, input width and parameter count as E-022's 3x3 (32,338,432), with the eight neighbours moved from touching the centre to a circle 222 km away. Radius chosen by measurement, not taste: ml/measure_ring_info.py puts the incremental one-step information a ring carries at its peak over 167-222 km (+1.6% of held-out residual variance vs +0.63% at one cell), because at one cell a neighbour correlates 0.968 with the centre and is nearly a copy of it. 222 km is the less redundant of the two peak radii (corr 0.718 vs 0.783). The ring is a circle on the GROUND: the zonal step is stretched by 1/cos(lat) per row. Controls already run: e022s9 (identical shape at 1 cell) and e017 (no neighbours). Pre-registered calibration: this probe predicted +0.63% at 1 cell where the real 3x3 delivered ~0%, so +1.6% is an upper bound against a weak linear baseline. Entry: ml/EXPERIMENTS.md E-023.",
